{"hash": "1fd12b7974b4136b", "text": "Most of those studios run a different kind of model, called diffusion. Picture a page of pure static. The model wipes away a little of the noise, step by step, each step nudged by your prompt, until a picture is left. The same trick makes images, video, sound effects and music, as far as their makers have said. Voices mostly aren't. Most current ones use a close cousin called flow matching, which needs fewer steps. Not every image model is diffusion, though. OpenAI's image models are reported to build pictures piece by piece, like text. And diffusion can write text, rarely. Inception's Mercury and Google's experimental diffusion models start from a smudged page and sharpen every word at once. Very fast, but not yet frontier quality. Every top chat model still writes one token after another. How generators work gets its own lesson in The Machine.", "alignment": {"characters": ["M", "o", "s", "t", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "o", "s", "e", " ", "s", "t", "u", "d", "i", "o", "s", " ", "r", "u", "n", " ", "a", " ", "d", "i", "f", "f", "e", "r", "e", "n", "t", " ", "k", "i", "n", "d", " ", "o", "f", " ", "m", "o", "d", "e", "l", ",", " ", "c", "a", "l", "l", "e", "d", " ", "d", "i", "f", "f", "u", "s", "i", "o", "n", ".", " ", "P", "i", "c", "t", "u", "r", "e", " ", "a", " ", "p", "a", "g", "e", " ", "o", "f", " ", "p", "u", "r", "e", " ", "s", "t", "a", "t", "i", "c", ".", " ", "T", "h", "e", " ", "m", "o", "d", "e", "l", " ", "w", "i", "p", "e", "s", " ", "a", "w", "a", "y", " ", "a", " ", "l", "i", "t", "t", "l", "e", " ", "o", "f", " ", "t", "h", "e", " ", "n", "o", "i", "s", "e", ",", " ", "s", "t", "e", "p", " ", "b", "y", " ", "s", "t", "e", "p", ",", " ", "e", "a", "c", "h", " ", "s", "t", "e", "p", " ", "n", "u", "d", "g", "e", "d", " ", "b", "y", " ", "y", "o", "u", "r", " ", "p", "r", "o", "m", "p", "t", ",", " ", "u", "n", "t", "i", "l", " ", "a", " ", "p", "i", "c", "t", "u", "r", "e", " ", "i", "s", " ", "l", "e", "f"